  <constraints>
    <constraint type="cost">Embedding cost is approximately $0.001 for a typical 10-50 article re-embed batch via Voyage AI. Total step cost is minimal. Voyage AI batch API supports up to 128 inputs per call.</constraint>
    <constraint type="timing">Execution time is approximately 3 seconds plus Voyage AI API call time. Timeout should be set to 60000ms to account for API latency. Memgraph upserts are fast (sub-second for typical batch sizes).</constraint>
    <constraint type="prerequisites">This step depends on infrastructure from three Epic 1 stories: Story 1.4 (lib/voyage-embed.mjs), Story 1.5 (graph-sync.mjs), Story 1.6 (S3 backup). If these are not deployed, the step should fail gracefully.</constraint>
    <constraint type="atomicity">compile-state.json must be written atomically (temp file + rename) to prevent corruption from partial writes. A corrupted state file would cause unnecessary re-embedding of all articles on the next run.</constraint>
    <constraint type="memgraph">Memgraph must be running on localhost:7687 for the sync to succeed. If Memgraph is down, graph-sync.mjs should log the error and preserve compile-state for the next attempt.</constraint>
    <constraint type="s3-backup">S3 backup is best-effort. Backup failures should be logged but should not fail the compile-sync step. The aws s3 sync command should use the --delete flag to keep S3 in sync with the local wiki.</constraint>
  </constraints>

